-- examples/checks/retract-again.rofl — A DELTA ASKED FOR AND THE WORLD EVALUATED AGAIN, WRITTEN IN THE WORLD. The
-- world retracts asks(ra_more) (the check's retract option): what a world asks names the rules it runs, so the Rust
-- engine evaluates again; it writes evaluated_again(Request, Reason) in the kernel's book, and a rule reads it. Rust
-- only: the TypeScript engine evaluates every change again and writes no row.
asks(ra_again).
asks(ra_more).
ra_name(ra_gone).
ra_more(R) :- ra_name(R).
ra_again(Why) :- evaluated_again(retract(_), Why).
-- expect-row: evaluated_again[$kernel](retract($fact(asks,main,$cons(ra_more,$nil))),"asks names the rules the world runs")
-- expect-row: ra_again[main]("asks names the rules the world runs")
